  "user_handle": "0xnija",
  "body": "## summary\nMissing zero-address validation for the `controller` parameter in request flows allows creation of requests that no one can claim or cancel, permanently locking user assets or shares.\n\n## Finding Description\nThe contract implements asynchronous request lifecycles keyed by `controller` across deposits and redeems. In `requestDeposit()` and `requestRedeem()`, the `controller` address is accepted without zero-address validation. Later claim and cancel functions authenticate strictly against `controller` (or its approved operator). If a request is created with `controller == address(0)`, there is no valid caller that can pass the `controller`-bound authentication, so the request can never transition to the Claimed state or be canceled. This results in permanent locking of funds.\n\n- Where requests are created without validating `controller`:\n  - `requestDeposit()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:341`\n  - `requestRedeem()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:715`\n- Where the authentication hard-binds to `controller`:\n  - `deposit()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:557`\n  - `mint()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:633`\n  - `cancelDepositRequest()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:1574`\n  - `claimCancelDepositRequest()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:1691`\n  - `cancelRedeemRequest()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:1745`\n  - `claimCancelRedeemRequest()` in `/2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol:1866`\n\nAdditionally, the zero-address is added to `activeDepositRequesters`/`activeRedeemRequesters`, polluting metrics and pagination, and reserved totals remain inflated.\n\n## Root cause:\nIn [`2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L341-371`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L341-L371) the `controller` is not validated against `address(0)` when creating deposit requests; similarly for redeems at [`2025-11-sukukfi/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L715-751`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L715-L751).\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L341-L371\n```solidity\nfunction requestDeposit(uint256 assets, address controller, address owner) external nonReentrant returns (uint256 requestId) {\n    if (!(owner == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(owner, msg.sender))) revert InvalidOwner();\n    if (assets == 0) revert ZeroAssets();\n    if (assets < $.minimumDepositAmount * (10 ** $.assetDecimals)) revert InsufficientDepositAmount();\n    SafeTokenTransfers.safeTransferFrom($.asset, owner, address(this), assets);\n    $.pendingDepositAssets[controller] += assets;\n    $.totalPendingDepositAssets += assets;\n    $.activeDepositRequesters.add(controller);\n    emit DepositRequest(controller, owner, REQUEST_ID, msg.sender, assets);\n    return REQUEST_ID;\n}\n```\nhttps://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/18fe2578cf1c6203dac7ff21513533010f3dda3e/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol#L715-L751\n```solidity\nfunction requestRedeem(uint256 shares, address controller, address owner) external nonReentrant returns (uint256 requestId) {\n    if (shares == 0) revert ZeroShares();\n    bool isOwnerOrOperator = owner == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(owner, msg.sender);\n    if (!isOwnerOrOperator) {\n        ShareTokenUpgradeable($.shareToken).spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares);\n    }\n    if (!ShareTokenUpgradeable($.shareToken).vaultTransferFrom(owner, address(this), shares)) revert ShareTransferFailed();\n    $.pendingRedeemShares[controller] += shares;\n    $.activeRedeemRequesters.add(controller);\n    emit RedeemRequest(controller, owner, REQUEST_ID, msg.sender, shares);\n    return REQUEST_ID;\n}\n```\n\nHighest-impact scenario: An approved operator or owner submits `requestDeposit()` or `requestRedeem()` with `controller == address(0)`. Assets or shares are pulled into the vault and recorded under the zero-address key. Even after fulfillment, no one can call `deposit()`, `mint()`, `redeem()`, `withdraw()`, or cancel/claim cancel functions because they require `controller == msg.sender` or its approved operator. As a result, funds remain stuck indefinitely.\n\n## Attack Path\n- Step 1: Call `requestDeposit(assets, controller=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000, owner)` or `requestRedeem(shares, controller=0x0, owner)`.\n- Step 2: Funds move into the vault; state records under `controller` key `0x0`.\n- Step 3: Manager fulfills to claimable; claim functions require `controller` authentication (`controller == msg.sender` or `isOperator(controller, msg.sender)`), which cannot be satisfied for `0x0`.\n- Step 4: Cancelation functions also require `controller` authentication; the `owner` cannot cancel. Funds are permanently locked.\n\n## Impact\nHigh. Permanent loss of access to user funds via unclaimable/un-cancelable requests and systemic state pollution; no viable recovery path without special admin intervention.\n\n## Recommendation\nValidate `controller` is non-zero on request entry points (and optionally validate `receiver` is non-zero in claim functions). If you need to support repairing misconfigured requests, provide a gated admin rescue that returns funds to the `owner` when `controller == address(0)`.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol b/src/ERC7575VaultUpgradeable.sol\n@@ function requestDeposit(uint256 assets, address controller, address owner) external nonReentrant returns (uint256 requestId) {\n-        if (!(owner == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(owner, msg.sender))) revert InvalidOwner();\n+        if (!(owner == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(owner, msg.sender))) revert InvalidOwner();\n+        if (controller == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n         if (assets == 0) revert ZeroAssets();\n@@ function requestRedeem(uint256 shares, address controller, address owner) external nonReentrant returns (uint256 requestId) {\n-        if (shares == 0) revert ZeroShares();\n+        if (shares == 0) revert ZeroShares();\n+        if (controller == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n         bool isOwnerOrOperator = owner == msg.sender || IERC7540($.shareToken).isOperator(owner, msg.sender);\n\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## poc \nAdded test in `test/ERC7575VaultUpgradeableCoverageTests.t.sol:330–360`\n```solidity\n    function testZeroAddressControllerLocksDeposit() public {\n        uint256 amount = 1000 * 1e18;\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        vault.requestDeposit(amount, address(0), user1);\n\n        uint256 pendingBefore = vault.pendingDepositRequest(0, address(0));\n        assertEq(pendingBefore, amount);\n\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        vault.cancelDepositRequest(0, address(0));\n\n        vault.fulfillDeposit(address(0), amount);\n\n        uint256 claimable = vault.claimableDepositRequest(0, address(0));\n        assertEq(claimable, amount);\n\n        vm.prank(user1);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        vault.deposit(amount, user1, address(0));\n\n        address[] memory reqs = vault.getActiveDepositRequesters();\n        bool found;\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < reqs.length; i++) {\n            if (reqs[i] == address(0)) {\n                found = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        assertTrue(found, \"zero address remains active requester\");\n    }\n```\n\n```c\nforge test -vv --match-test testZeroAddressControllerLocksDeposit\n```",
